title The law counts by function and every instrument counted by file
prompt autonomous lap -- GRASS auditing lane, TAME Guidance pass
rota lap 4510, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels; advanced by hand past row 0, which this ship read at 20260910.012314 the same day. Air asks where each thing ends, and its test is to pull on a part: TAME root rule 2 states its aim in FUNCTIONS, so I ran a hand along that fence and it gave way.
think Read the card whole, launched the cold roster detached, then searched what stands over TAME root rule 2. Four instruments: assert_gap and invariant_gap ask a FILE question, unnamed_assert and invariant_coverage_scan bins ask a per-ASSERT question. None asks the per-FUNCTION question the law itself spells -- "aim >= two per function".
think Probed before building. A copy of invariant_coverage_scan.sh patched in .lap/ read 23,319 contract functions with 3,814 meeting the aim, 16 percent, against contract_coverage_percent=97 from the same run. Two honest numbers answering two questions.
think Built the reading INTO invariant_coverage_scan.sh rather than beside it. Its function walk, proof-reachability spread, and five assert-call exclusions already stood there; a sibling scan would be a second answer to what a contract function is -- the braid single-stranded names, which is this row's fixed seat.
think Added a functions mode ranking a module by its own unguarded count, so the census is usable locally rather than only as a tree total.
obs The control caught my own plant. Leg 12 put two asserts on one line and read one, because both readings count assert LINES rather than CALLS. Rather than adding a second counting rule I named the granularity and measured it: 2 lines tree-wide carry two calls across 1,964 sources, so line counting is exact within two. Leg 12a keeps that limit visible.
obs The nested-declaration blind spot is counted rather than described -- fn_nested_unread reads 1,224 over the contract population, and a tree-wide grep reads 1,839 of 34,241 declarations. Two populations, two figures, both printed. Widening the column-0 anchor would move the proof classification the control's fifteen elder legs were built around, so this lap leaves the anchor alone.
obs Gates nothing, deliberately. The law says aim, and a ceiling at 16 percent would red the tree on the lap it landed -- a gate that reds on ordinary work is a gate somebody turns off.
obs The cold roster reached 57 of roughly 217 guards in 45 minutes with six peer passes running and load 12.8, so this lap proved on named guards rather than voiding the pass or claiming a green it never read.
loom guard=invariant_coverage_scan wall_ms=13252 modules=1734 contract_functions=23319 fn_two_or_more=3814
